\DOC UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC

\TYPE {UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes a goal whose conclusion equates an explicit event-list expression with
an application of an uninterpreted event-list function to arguments, leaving no
subgoals.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. Applied to a goal {A ?- t = u} in which {t} is a concrete
list (or an {APPEND} of concrete lists and other event-list terms) and {u} is a
call of a function symbol to arguments, it discharges the goal entirely,
leaving {A} untouched — nothing added, nothing removed, no residual subgoal:
{
      A ?- t = u
      ==========  UNIFY_F_EVENTS_TAC
}
{
   
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces the inputs are uniformly goals of this event-list
equality form, under large assumption lists describing machine states, and the
single outcome shown is the tactic closing the goal.

\ENDDOC
